# ripgrep's settings. ripgrep (rg) searches through file contents. It reads this
# file only because RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH in ~/.config/zsh/.zshenv points to it.
# One ripgrep option per line (see GUIDE.md, "Configuration file").

# Case-insensitive unless the pattern has an uppercase letter.
--smart-case

# Search hidden files and directories (e.g. dotfiles), but never inside .git.
# (--glob=!PATTERN skips the files that match PATTERN.)
--hidden
--glob=!.git/*

# Don't print huge lines (e.g. minified files); show a preview of them instead.
--max-columns=150
--max-columns-preview
